This constraint is about the whole header rather than `ClientId`. I’d move it up to the version history comment above `validVersions`, where the next header version will be added.
```
  // Version 3 introduces ClientInstanceId. (KIP-1313)
  //
  // Compatibility constraints:
  // - New header fields must be tagged until every broker version that clients are required to
  //   support (see KIP-896) includes the fix from KAFKA-21160 (first shipped in 4.5.0).
  // - The first four fields (RequestApiKey, RequestApiVersion, CorrelationId, ClientId) must keep
  //   their order and encoding across all versions.
  // - Version 1 must not be removed. Brokers use it to parse headers with an unsupported API version.
  // See RequestHeader#parse for details.
  "validVersions": "1-3",
```

